> >> I'm seriously considering reverse genociding purple worms repeatedly
> >> when I hit the first plane, and whistling them through :)

They're not too great on the four planes - elementals are too large to
be swallowed, which means your purple worms will end up getting hit by
earth elementals and taking fire damage from fire elementals which can
considerably stunt their longevity. The best place for a purple worm
is the astral plane, as both priests and angels are small and
low-level enough to get swallowed. I had one there when i finally did
another ascension sunday (neutral priestess of Chih-Sung-Tzu), and
though it didn't make it - tried nibbling on a dragon for too long -
it greatly helped clearing out the astral plane. My prize pet was,
however, the only Archon i ever encountered that game - tamed on the
first try with a spell of charm monster.

> >So, you obviously remembered how to get to the top of the
> >wizards tower.
> 
> I think so.  I'll be trying tonight.

I wish you luck. Or rather, i wish you won't need any luck (skill
trumps luck 10 times out of 10). 

> >As to your dastardly purple worm campaign, I'd save it for
> >Astral and then use conflict to spice things up even more!
> 
> But then they might eat each other!

No. Purple worms are too large to be swallowed. However, they might
end up swallowing the riders, which inevitably instakills the hapless
munchkinish creature. They don't need conflict as encouragement,
anyway - purple worms are high-level enough to assault pretty much
anything you can encounter on Astral.

> and I *can* get them from plane to plane by whistling by the portal,
> can't I?

Yes. Unless they're currently busy eating.

